# tally 2.2.1 P30 (L §4.4 l.667 to l.671): an operation decides over an interval only what holds for every value
# the interval can hold; its ends stand for them only where it is monotone and gives a value everywhere between.
# N5: start_of and end_of of month_of(wx), wx across February and March, are monotone and total, so their ends:
# window(2026-02-01, 2026-03-01) and window(2026-03-01, 2026-04-01); so_c compares that computed interval with wx, two
# unknowns, the hole. tally 2.2 printed the hole for a print, REFCORE-NOT-YET and RUN-DOMAIN.
=== so.tally
model so
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source card "invented"
input wx: date
version v_card
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  wx = window(2026-02-20, 2026-03-10) "c"
ask so: start_of(month_of(wx))
ask eo: end_of(month_of(wx))
ask mo: month_of(wx)
ask yo: start_of(year_of(wx))
ask so_c: start_of(month_of(wx)) <= wx
=== expect
eo: window(2026-03-01, 2026-04-01)
  cut 2026-01-01
mo: ?"date within window(2026-02-20, 2026-03-10) not precise enough for a print" (wx)
  unknown day: wx
  cut 2026-01-01
so: window(2026-02-01, 2026-03-01)
  cut 2026-01-01
so_c: ?"date within window(2026-02-20, 2026-03-10) not precise enough for start_of(month_of(wx)) <= wx" (wx)
  unknown day: wx
  cut 2026-01-01
yo: 2026-01-01
  cut 2026-01-01
